---
const canonicalUrl = 'https://superada.ai/max-ai-vertical-ops-product-brief-v1/';
const heroImage = '/images/unlisted/max-ai/max-ai-brief-v2-ui-reference.png';

const verticals = [
  { rank: '01', name: 'HVAC', note: 'Top home-service wedge. High inbound volume, existing software spend, clear automation ROI.' },
  { rank: '02', name: 'Plumbing', note: 'Similar scheduling, dispatch, job-context, and customer-update pain.' },
  { rank: '03', name: 'Electrical', note: 'Field workflow, appointment, quote, and follow-up patterns map cleanly to an internal assistant.' },
  { rank: '04', name: 'Property Management', note: 'Lots of calls, texts, maintenance coordination, vendor routing, and resident updates.' },
  { rank: '05', name: 'Insurance Agencies', note: 'Contrarian wedge: proof of insurance, add a vehicle, certificates, billing questions, strong margins.' },
  { rank: '06', name: 'Real Estate Teams', note: 'Short-cycle communication, lead follow-up, scheduling, transaction coordination, and status updates.' },
];

const names = [
  'FieldMax',
  'ServicePilot',
  'JobBrain',
  'CrewCopilot',
  'Dispatch Agent',
  'Max for Trades',
  'RouteReady',
  'ShopMind',
  'OnCall Ops',
  'ServiceDesk AI',
];

const nextSteps = [
  'Choose the first vertical using warm distribution as the deciding factor.',
  'Prioritize HVAC, plumbing, and electrical, with in-home appliance repair kept alive if the voice-memo distribution path is real.',
  'Write a one-page pilot offer for 3 to 5 businesses: free for 60 to 90 days, internal assistant only, paid only after value is proven.',
  'Define the first four workflows: next appointment, parts to order, job and customer context, follow-up reminders.',
  'Map the required systems for the first pilot: schedule, customer records, job notes, parts data, calls, texts, and message history.',
  'Build the smallest internal assistant that can answer useful daily questions from real business data.',
  'Measure usage before satisfaction: repeat questions, daily use, saved follow-ups, and operator reliance.',
  'Test the first paid conversion around $100 per month only after the pilot has real usage.',
  'Keep insurance agencies on the test list as a contrarian high-margin wedge, especially if a warm intro appears.',
  'Defer the customer-facing agent until internal trust is visible.',
];
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex,nofollow,noarchive" />
    <link rel="canonical" href={canonicalUrl} />
    <title>Max AI Vertical Ops Assistant | Product Brief v2</title>
    <style is:inline>
      :root {
        color-scheme: dark;
        --bg: oklch(0.145 0.035 265);
        --bg-2: oklch(0.105 0.03 265);
        --surface: oklch(0.19 0.04 263 / 0.88);
        --surface-strong: oklch(0.235 0.052 263 / 0.92);
        --surface-soft: oklch(0.255 0.055 263 / 0.48);
        --ink: oklch(0.975 0.015 250);
        --muted: oklch(0.78 0.035 255);
        --faint: oklch(0.62 0.045 255);
        --line: oklch(0.38 0.065 255 / 0.72);
        --primary: oklch(0.82 0.105 82);
        --accent: oklch(0.72 0.105 198);
        --green: oklch(0.78 0.15 152);
        --rose: oklch(0.73 0.16 12);
        --shadow: 0 28px 80px oklch(0.02 0.02 265 / 0.46);
        --radius: 1.35rem;
        --font-sans: Inter, ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
        --font-display: Georgia, "Times New Roman", ui-serif, serif;
      }

      * { box-sizing: border-box; }
      html { scroll-behavior: smooth; }
      body {
        margin: 0;
        min-height: 100vh;
        color: var(--ink);
        font-family: var(--font-sans);
        line-height: 1.58;
        background:
          radial-gradient(circle at 15% 0%, oklch(0.38 0.1 260 / 0.9), transparent 34rem),
          radial-gradient(circle at 85% 10%, oklch(0.38 0.12 190 / 0.52), transparent 30rem),
          linear-gradient(180deg, var(--bg), var(--bg-2) 72%);
      }
      body:before {
        content: "";
        position: fixed;
        inset: 0;
        pointer-events: none;
        background-image: linear-gradient(oklch(1 0 0 / 0.035) 1px, transparent 1px), linear-gradient(90deg, oklch(1 0 0 / 0.035) 1px, transparent 1px);
        background-size: 42px 42px;
        mask-image: linear-gradient(to bottom, black, transparent 72%);
      }
      a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; }
      a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
      .wrap { width: min(1180px, calc(100% - 32px)); margin: 0 auto; }
      .hero-art { padding-top: 2rem; }
      .hero-art-frame { position: relative; overflow: hidden; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: calc(var(--radius) + 0.2rem); background: oklch(0.11 0.03 265 / 0.88); box-shadow: var(--shadow); }
      .hero-art-frame:before { content: ""; position: absolute; inset: 0; pointer-events: none; background: linear-gradient(180deg, oklch(1 0 0 / 0.08), transparent 18%, transparent 78%, oklch(0 0 0 / 0.18)); z-index: 1; }
      .hero-art-frame img { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; }
      .hero-art-caption { margin: 0.6rem 0 0; color: var(--faint); font-size: 0.82rem; text-align: right; }
      .hero { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.15fr) minmax(320px, 0.85fr); gap: 1rem; padding: 1rem 0 1rem; }
      .panel {
        border: 1px solid var(--line);
        border-radius: var(--radius);
        background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--surface), oklch(0.13 0.035 263 / 0.9));
        box-shadow: var(--shadow);
        backdrop-filter: blur(18px);
      }
      .hero-main { padding: clamp(1.35rem, 4vw, 2.6rem); position: relative; overflow: hidden; }
      .hero-main:after {
        content: "";
        position: absolute;
        width: 22rem;
        height: 22rem;
        border-radius: 999px;
        right: -9rem;
        top: -9rem;
        background: radial-gradient(circle, oklch(0.82 0.142 83 / 0.18), transparent 68%);
      }
      .eyebrow { color: var(--primary); font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 900; letter-spacing: 0.16em; text-transform: uppercase; }
      h1 { max-width: 860px; margin: 0.8rem 0 1rem; font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: clamp(3rem, 7.8vw, 6.6rem); font-weight: 700; line-height: 0.9; letter-spacing: -0.075em; }
      .thesis { max-width: 760px; color: oklch(0.91 0.027 250); font-size: clamp(1.08rem, 2vw, 1.45rem); }
      .pillrow { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.55rem; margin-top: 1.35rem; }
      .pill { border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 999px; padding: 0.52rem 0.72rem; background: oklch(0.24 0.045 263 / 0.74); color: oklch(0.88 0.03 250); font-size: 0.83rem; font-weight: 800; }
      .copybar { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.65rem; margin-top: 1.45rem; }
      button, .button { min-height: 44px; border: 0; border-radius: 999px; padding: 0.74rem 1rem; cursor: pointer; background: var(--primary); color: oklch(0.16 0.045 83); font-weight: 900; }
      button.secondary { border: 1px solid var(--line); background: oklch(0.2 0.042 263 / 0.82); color: var(--ink); }
      .signal-stack { display: grid; gap: 0.75rem; padding: 1rem; }
      .signal { border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 1rem; padding: 1rem; background: oklch(0.13 0.035 263 / 0.72); transition: transform 180ms ease, border-color 180ms ease; }
      .signal:hover { transform: translateY(-2px); border-color: oklch(0.72 0.15 205 / 0.82); }
      .signal b { display: block; color: var(--primary); font-size: 1.7rem; line-height: 1; letter-spacing: -0.035em; }
      .signal span { display: block; margin-top: 0.45rem; color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.92rem; }
      .nav { position: sticky; top: 0; z-index: 20; margin-top: 0.5rem; border-block: 1px solid var(--line); background: oklch(0.11 0.03 265 / 0.86); backdrop-filter: blur(16px); }
      .nav-inner { width: min(1180px, calc(100% - 32px)); margin: 0 auto; padding: 0.65rem 0; display: flex; gap: 0.55rem; overflow-x: auto; }
      .nav a { white-space: nowrap; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 999px; padding: 0.5rem 0.75rem; color: oklch(0.86 0.03 250); background: oklch(0.2 0.042 263 / 0.72); font-size: 0.82rem; font-weight: 850; }
      main { padding: 1.4rem 0 3.5rem; }
      .callouts { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 1rem; }
      .callout { padding: 1.15rem; }
      .tag { display: inline-flex; border-radius: 999px; padding: 0.3rem 0.55rem; margin-bottom: 0.7rem; font-size: 0.72rem; font-weight: 950; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; }
      .tag.go { color: oklch(0.9 0.15 150); background: oklch(0.28 0.09 150 / 0.55); }
      .tag.warn { color: oklch(0.9 0.11 83); background: oklch(0.32 0.09 83 / 0.48); }
      .section { position: relative; margin-top: 1rem; padding: clamp(1.15rem, 3vw, 1.7rem); overflow: hidden; }
      .section:before { content: ""; position: absolute; inset: 0 0 auto; height: 3px; background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--primary), var(--accent), var(--green)); }
      .kicker { color: var(--primary); font-size: 0.72rem; font-weight: 950; letter-spacing: 0.18em; text-transform: uppercase; }
      h2 { margin: 0.35rem 0 0.8rem; font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: clamp(1.7rem, 3vw, 2.55rem); font-weight: 700; line-height: 1; letter-spacing: -0.045em; }
      h3 { margin: 1rem 0 0.35rem; font-size: 1.12rem; }
      p { margin: 0 0 0.8rem; color: oklch(0.82 0.032 250); }
      ul, ol { margin: 0.7rem 0 0; padding-left: 1.25rem; color: oklch(0.82 0.032 250); }
      li { margin: 0.45rem 0; }
      strong { color: white; }
      .vertical-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 0.8rem; margin-top: 1rem; }
      .vertical-card { min-height: 10.5rem; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 1rem; padding: 1rem; background: linear-gradient(180deg, oklch(0.2 0.045 263 / 0.76), oklch(0.13 0.035 263 / 0.78)); transition: transform 180ms ease, border-color 180ms ease; }
      .vertical-card:hover { transform: translateY(-3px); border-color: oklch(0.82 0.142 83 / 0.82); }
      .vertical-card .rank { color: var(--primary); font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 950; letter-spacing: 0.12em; }
      .vertical-card h3 { margin-top: 0.35rem; font-size: 1.22rem; }
      .criteria { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 0.65rem; margin-top: 0.9rem; padding: 0; list-style: none; }
      .criteria li { margin: 0; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 0.85rem; padding: 0.7rem 0.75rem; background: oklch(0.14 0.035 263 / 0.65); color: oklch(0.86 0.028 250); }
      .names { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 0.65rem; padding: 0; list-style: none; }
      .names li { margin: 0; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 0.95rem; padding: 0.85rem 0.9rem; background: oklch(0.14 0.035 263 / 0.72); color: white; font-weight: 850; }
      .structured-list { display: grid; gap: 0.7rem; margin-top: 0.9rem; padding: 0; list-style: none; }
      .structured-list li { margin: 0; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 1rem; padding: 0.86rem 0.95rem; background: oklch(0.145 0.038 263 / 0.72); }
      .structured-list strong { display: block; margin-bottom: 0.18rem; }
      .numbered-list { counter-reset: step; display: grid; gap: 0.7rem; margin-top: 0.9rem; padding: 0; list-style: none; }
      .numbered-list li { counter-increment: step; position: relative; margin: 0; min-height: 3.25rem; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 1rem; padding: 0.84rem 0.95rem 0.84rem 3.3rem; background: oklch(0.145 0.038 263 / 0.72); }
      .numbered-list li:before { content: counter(step, decimal-leading-zero); position: absolute; left: 0.85rem; top: 0.85rem; color: var(--primary); font-size: 0.76rem; font-weight: 950; letter-spacing: 0.08em; }
      .question-list { columns: 2; column-gap: 2rem; margin-top: 0.8rem; }
      .question-list li { break-inside: avoid; }
      .subgrid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 0.8rem; margin-top: 1rem; }
      .subcard { border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 1rem; padding: 1rem; background: oklch(0.14 0.035 263 / 0.68); }
      .subcard h3 { margin-top: 0; }
      .handoff-strip { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 0.7rem; margin-top: 1rem; padding: 0; list-style: none; }
      .handoff-strip li { position: relative; min-height: 6.2rem; margin: 0; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 1rem; padding: 0.92rem; background: oklch(0.14 0.035 263 / 0.7); }
      .handoff-strip li:after { content: ""; position: absolute; top: 50%; right: -0.7rem; width: 0.7rem; border-top: 1px dashed oklch(0.72 0.105 198 / 0.68); }
      .handoff-strip li:last-child { border-color: oklch(0.82 0.105 82 / 0.8); background: oklch(0.22 0.055 83 / 0.42); }
      .handoff-strip li:last-child:after { display: none; }
      .handoff-strip b { display: block; color: var(--accent); margin-bottom: 0.2rem; font-size: 0.76rem; letter-spacing: 0.12em; text-transform: uppercase; }
      .handoff-strip li:last-child b { color: var(--primary); }
      .footer { margin-top: 1.2rem; padding: 1rem 0 0; color: var(--faint); font-size: 0.84rem; }
      @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { html { scroll-behavior: auto; } .signal, .vertical-card { transition: none; } .signal:hover, .vertical-card:hover { transform: none; } }
      @media (max-width: 920px) { .hero, .callouts, .vertical-grid, .criteria, .subgrid, .handoff-strip { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .handoff-strip li:after { display: none; } .signal-stack { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); } .question-list { columns: 1; } }
      @media (max-width: 620px) { .wrap, .nav-inner { width: min(100% - 24px, 1180px); } .signal-stack, .names { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .hero { padding-top: 1rem; } h1 { font-size: 3rem; } }
      @media print { body { background: white; color: #111; } body:before, .nav, .copybar { display: none; } .panel, .vertical-card, .criteria li, .names li { box-shadow: none; background: white; color: #111; } p, li, .signal span { color: #111; } }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <section class="wrap hero-art" aria-label="V2 UI reference image">
      <figure class="hero-art-frame">
        <img src={heroImage} alt="Max AI Vertical Ops Assistant V2 UI reference showing the premium operator dashboard direction and vertical prioritization cards" loading="eager" decoding="async" />
      </figure>
      <p class="hero-art-caption">Image taste reference used for the v2 page direction.</p>
    </section>

    <header class="wrap hero">
      <section class="hero-main panel" aria-labelledby="page-title">
        <div class="eyebrow">Unlisted SuperAda product brief · v2</div>
        <h1 id="page-title">Max AI Vertical Ops Assistant</h1>
        <p class="thesis">Max AI should not start as “AI for everyone.” The practical wedge is an internal AI ops assistant for vertical service businesses: help the owner, dispatcher, or technician move faster first, then turn the same trusted context into the customer-facing agent later.</p>
        <div class="pillrow" aria-label="Positioning tags">
          <span class="pill">Internal ops first</span>
          <span class="pill">Customer agent second</span>
          <span class="pill">B2B now</span>
          <span class="pill">B2B2C later</span>
          <span class="pill">HVAC · Plumbing · Electrical</span>
          <span class="pill">Insurance as contrarian wedge</span>
        </div>
        <div class="copybar">
          <button type="button" onclick="location.href='#next-steps'">Jump to next steps</button>
          <button type="button" class="secondary" onclick="window.print()">Print / Save PDF</button>
        </div>
      </section>
      <aside class="panel signal-stack" aria-label="Brief signals">
        <div class="signal"><b>6</b><span>Priority verticals from Andy’s post: HVAC, plumbing, electrical, property management, insurance agencies, real estate teams.</span></div>
        <div class="signal"><b>3 to 5</b><span>Warm businesses to pilot before building a platform story.</span></div>
        <div class="signal"><b>60 to 90</b><span>Free pilot days before asking for payment.</span></div>
        <div class="signal"><b>$100/mo</b><span>Rough first paid price anchor, only after usage proves value.</span></div>
      </aside>
    </header>

    <nav class="nav" aria-label="Page navigation">
      <div class="nav-inner">
        <a href="#problem">Problem</a>
        <a href="#andy-screen">Andy’s screen</a>
        <a href="#recommendation">Recommendation</a>
        <a href="#concept">Concept</a>
        <a href="#mvp">MVP</a>
        <a href="#gtm">GTM</a>
        <a href="#risks">Risks</a>
        <a href="#names">Names</a>
        <a href="#next-steps">Next steps</a>
      </div>
    </nav>

    <main class="wrap">
      <div class="callouts">
        <section class="callout panel">
          <span class="tag go">Recommendation</span>
          <h2>Start where distribution is warmest, not where the idea feels biggest.</h2>
          <p>Andy’s execution advice is the strategic constraint: talk less, do more, pick a segment, launch fast, and let pilot usage tell the truth.</p>
        </section>
        <section class="callout panel">
          <span class="tag warn">Update from Andy’s post</span>
          <h2>HVAC, plumbing, and electrical move to the top of the home-service list.</h2>
          <p>Insurance agencies become the contrarian test: repetitive communication, strong margins, modernizing stacks, and less obvious competition.</p>
        </section>
      </div>

      <section id="problem" class="panel section">
        <div class="kicker">01 · Problem</div>
        <h2>The network product is the destination, not the starting point.</h2>
        <p>The voice memo produced three credible business-model paths. V2 makes the distinction explicit so the page reads like a product brief instead of a long memo.</p>
        <ol class="numbered-list">
          <li><strong>B2C:</strong> sell Max AI directly to consumers. Highest long-term surface area, but the hardest path for trust, integrations, and distribution.</li>
          <li><strong>B2B:</strong> sell workflow software to businesses first. Best starting motion because it can prove value with a small pilot.</li>
          <li><strong>B2B2C:</strong> businesses pay, customers eventually recognize and reuse Max AI across many providers. This is the Shopify plus Shop destination.</li>
        </ol>
        <h3>The first operational pain</h3>
        <p>Vertical service businesses already live inside messy scheduling systems, job notes, calls, texts, parts questions, and follow-up reminders. Owners and technicians need quick answers:</p>
        <ul class="question-list">
          <li>What is my next appointment?</li>
          <li>What happened with this customer?</li>
          <li>What parts should we order?</li>
          <li>Who needs a follow-up?</li>
          <li>What should I tell the customer now?</li>
          <li>Which jobs need attention today?</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="andy-screen" class="panel section">
        <div class="kicker">02 · Andy’s vertical screen</div>
        <h2>The new priority list is more useful than the abstract category map.</h2>
        <p>Andy’s post gives a concrete screen for picking the first market. If he were building the company from scratch today, he would prioritize these verticals:</p>
        <div class="vertical-grid">
          {verticals.map((vertical) => (
            <article class="vertical-card">
              <div class="rank">{vertical.rank}</div>
              <h3>{vertical.name}</h3>
              <p>{vertical.note}</p>
            </article>
          ))}
        </div>
        <h3>Why these six qualify</h3>
        <ul class="criteria">
          <li>Already buy communication tools</li>
          <li>Already buy software</li>
          <li>Have APIs available</li>
          <li>Have lots of inbound calls and texts</li>
          <li>Have measurable ROI from automation</li>
          <li>Have relatively short sales cycles</li>
        </ul>
        <p>That screen changes the brief. HVAC, plumbing, and electrical should sit at the top of the first-pass home-service list. Insurance agencies should not be ignored. They have repetitive communication like proof of insurance, add a vehicle, certificate requests, billing questions, and routine updates, plus strong margins and increasingly modern software stacks.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="recommendation" class="panel section">
        <div class="kicker">03 · Recommendation</div>
        <h2>Start B2B in one vertical. Design for B2B2C later.</h2>
        <h3>Default priority order</h3>
        <ol class="numbered-list">
          <li><strong>HVAC:</strong> top home-service wedge from Andy’s post.</li>
          <li><strong>Plumbing:</strong> same appointment, dispatch, follow-up, and customer-context pattern.</li>
          <li><strong>Electrical:</strong> field workflow and job-context pain map cleanly to an internal assistant.</li>
          <li><strong>In-home appliance repair:</strong> keep alive if the warm distribution path from the voice memo is real.</li>
          <li><strong>Insurance agencies:</strong> contrarian high-margin test with repetitive communication and modernizing stacks.</li>
        </ol>
        <h3>Product sequence</h3>
        <ol class="numbered-list">
          <li>Internal AI ops assistant first.</li>
          <li>Customer-facing agent second.</li>
          <li>Cross-business Max AI identity only after the product is trusted inside the business.</li>
        </ol>
      </section>

      <section id="concept" class="panel section">
        <div class="kicker">04 · Product concept</div>
        <h2>Max AI is the operating brain for a vertical service business.</h2>
        <ol class="handoff-strip" aria-label="Internal assistant to customer handoff">
          <li><b>Capture</b>Connect schedule, job notes, parts, calls, texts, and customer records.</li>
          <li><b>Assist</b>Help the owner, dispatcher, or technician answer daily operational questions.</li>
          <li><b>Trust</b>Measure repeat usage before exposing the assistant to customers.</li>
          <li><b>Handoff</b>Use the same context for booking, status, reminders, availability, and basic job questions.</li>
        </ol>
        <div class="subgrid">
          <article class="subcard">
            <h3>Internal assistant first</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Connects to existing operational systems.</li>
              <li>Serves the owner, dispatcher, or technician during the workday.</li>
              <li>Answers questions before, during, and after a job.</li>
            </ul>
          </article>
          <article class="subcard">
            <h3>Customer layer second</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Uses the same trusted business context.</li>
              <li>Handles booking, status, reminders, and availability.</li>
              <li>Creates the path toward the long-term B2B2C Max AI surface.</li>
            </ul>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="mvp" class="panel section">
        <div class="kicker">05 · MVP</div>
        <h2>One vertical. One business workflow. One daily usage test.</h2>
        <h3>Pilot shape</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>3 to 5 warm businesses.</li>
          <li>One starting vertical.</li>
          <li>First 60 to 90 days free.</li>
          <li>Paid conversion only after value is proven.</li>
          <li>Possible first price anchor around $100 per month, subject to actual willingness to pay.</li>
        </ul>
        <h3>Workflow scope</h3>
        <ol>
          <li>Next appointment lookup.</li>
          <li>Parts-to-order support.</li>
          <li>Job and customer context summary.</li>
          <li>Follow-up reminders and draft messages.</li>
        </ol>
        <h3>Product constraints</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>No broad marketplace.</li>
          <li>No consumer app first.</li>
          <li>No generic AI platform pitch.</li>
          <li>No customer-facing bot until internal users trust the assistant.</li>
          <li>No claim that one vertical proves all verticals.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="gtm" class="panel section">
        <div class="kicker">06 · GTM</div>
        <h2>The first proof is not a deck. It is a business using the assistant during the workday.</h2>
        <ol class="numbered-list">
          <li><strong>Pick by warm access:</strong> choose the vertical with the strongest distribution path, not the prettiest market map.</li>
          <li><strong>Get 3 to 5 pilots live:</strong> keep the first cohort small enough to support manually.</li>
          <li><strong>Sell the business outcome:</strong> fewer dropped follow-ups, faster job context, clearer parts planning, better customer communication.</li>
          <li><strong>Run 60 to 90 days free:</strong> let usage form before price pressure.</li>
          <li><strong>Convert after repeated use:</strong> test a simple paid plan around $100 per month only after value is visible.</li>
          <li><strong>Expand inside one vertical:</strong> do not jump categories until one wedge shows repeatable usage.</li>
          <li><strong>Keep insurance as a parallel test:</strong> use it if a warm intro appears because communication volume and margins may justify a different wedge.</li>
        </ol>
      </section>

      <section id="risks" class="panel section">
        <div class="kicker">07 · Risks and falsifiers</div>
        <h2>Kill the idea quickly if the usage signal is fake.</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Distribution risk:</strong> the warm path may not produce real pilot access. Falsifier: 3 to 5 warm businesses will not try the product even when the first 60 to 90 days are free.</li>
          <li><strong>Usage risk:</strong> operators may like the demo but not change daily behavior. Falsifier: technicians, dispatchers, or owners do not ask repeat questions after the first week.</li>
          <li><strong>Integration risk:</strong> the tools in the target vertical may be harder to connect than expected. Falsifier: the MVP cannot answer next appointment, job context, or follow-up questions from available systems within the pilot window.</li>
          <li><strong>Pricing risk:</strong> $100 per month may be too low for the work required or too high for perceived value. Falsifier: pilots use the product but will not convert after value is shown.</li>
          <li><strong>Sequencing risk:</strong> launching the customer-facing agent too early could create trust and accuracy problems. Falsifier: internal users are not willing to rely on the assistant before customers see it.</li>
          <li><strong>Vertical-transfer risk:</strong> insurance agencies may require a different workflow and sales motion than home services. Falsifier: a small insurance-agency test shows the communication pain is real, but the buying motion or integration surface does not transfer.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

